{"title":"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 17","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Alternate_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Alternate Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/e/8be90c4c2c281e2298292cbc415bcb6e08019586.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + ar_1 + ar_1^2 + ar_1^3 + \\cdots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"195\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/f/4ff4c53a44b64ff99685cb7814fabc9abfac2828.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + ar_2 + ar_2^2 + ar_2^3 + \\cdots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"195\" height=\"19\" /> be two different infinite geometric series of positive numbers with the same first term.  The sum of the first series is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/c/adc143c3f887fa7e92fd80d91bb22af51b4abd77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" />, and the sum of the second series is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/4/0b4f3f4b698ce35667432041e168f7653533fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" />.  What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/3/9338efce1e9efab973711535ac35105f76563762.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1 + r_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/c/56c539aef3d61e416b7c9cf880277f4998e9b379.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 0\\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac {1}{2}\\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 1\\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac {1 + \\sqrt {5}}{2}\\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"403\" height=\"41\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using the formula for the sum of a geometric series we get that the sums of the given two sequences are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/9/6d949cab5e29cb9eacb58ef6fdaa5c105a015eb0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac a{1-r_1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"49\" height=\"35\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/5/de57026814801e0fbc038aaa54d16a6b9f70c058.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac a{1-r_2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"49\" height=\"35\" />. \n</p><p>Hence we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/9/689e152b77560dd68e67e9dac8b5cf1fd819382e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac a{1-r_1} = r_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"88\" height=\"35\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/0/53089e4f85f602d2d7f5b7fad83863be4cc9519b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac a{1-r_2} = r_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"89\" height=\"35\" />.\nThis can be rewritten as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/0/050a5a38993e4934023e4bffec0032bdc02de781.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1(1-r_1) = r_2(1-r_2) = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"211\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p>As we are given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/c/adc143c3f887fa7e92fd80d91bb22af51b4abd77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/4/0b4f3f4b698ce35667432041e168f7653533fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> are distinct, these must be precisely the two roots of the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/d/1ed95bf4e1196cb72ef474469448272dc6b9bd32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 - x + a = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"115\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Using <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Vieta%27s_formulas\" title=\"Vieta&#39;s formulas\">Vieta's formulas</a> we get that the sum of these two roots is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/4/3547351abf03ab0b6cbda7b0b905b2e4f6220e1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"20\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using the previous solution we reach the equality <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/3/df3ab66eb44ee62c29c78f1f74624c1930980198.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1(1-r_1) = r_2(1-r_2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"180\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Obviously, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/3/b63b7ce92ddb3ab52411b72210a4a4794e85e73d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1 \\neq r_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/5/3c50e493bef732de04b8a3aaae0763f812cc3f8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1 = 1 - r_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"89\" height=\"17\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/5/7357ea1176963eeb7a9c1a25d79d539d73f8c3b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1 + r_2 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"89\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n-Vignesh Peddi\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We basically have two infinite geometric series whose sum is equivalent to the common ratio. Let us have a geometric series: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/4/eb4a8e7fa93e80377aea2129c54b49fcc75444c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b, br, br^2.....$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"87\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p>The sum is: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/9/0596e08d84e91fbe79163af931c3a373bb566c67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{b}{1-r} = r.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"79\" height=\"38\" /> Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/c/7ec84c04fd03ad77cfaa76a379aa0541f86bc52c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = r-r^2$\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" /> and by Vieta's, the sum of the two possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/c/adc143c3f887fa7e92fd80d91bb22af51b4abd77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/4/0b4f3f4b698ce35667432041e168f7653533fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" />) is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p>~conantwiz2023\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Alternate_Solution\">Alternate Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Alternate Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using the formula for the sum of a geometric series we get that the sums of the given two sequences are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/9/6d949cab5e29cb9eacb58ef6fdaa5c105a015eb0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac a{1-r_1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"49\" height=\"35\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/5/de57026814801e0fbc038aaa54d16a6b9f70c058.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac a{1-r_2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"49\" height=\"35\" />. \n</p><p>Hence we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/9/689e152b77560dd68e67e9dac8b5cf1fd819382e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac a{1-r_1} = r_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"88\" height=\"35\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/0/53089e4f85f602d2d7f5b7fad83863be4cc9519b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac a{1-r_2} = r_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"89\" height=\"35\" />.\nThis can be rewritten as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/0/050a5a38993e4934023e4bffec0032bdc02de781.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1(1-r_1) = r_2(1-r_2) = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"211\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Which can be further rewritten as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/e/2cea29d8ae27b85213a563736776339ebc0869b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1-r_1^2 = r_2-r_2^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"131\" height=\"19\" />.\nRearranging the equation we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/1/fb19a3d00d52ea14fe0c8eda6915b2a6ce7a3231.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1-r_2 = r_1^2-r_2^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"131\" height=\"19\" />.\nExpressing this as a difference of squares we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/3/be31e8842862a3c45543f522558f9d11a29d12d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1-r_2 = (r_1-r_2)(r_1+r_2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"211\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Dividing by like terms we finally get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/9/a4916571b4c31c84c1226806fc695c2798677a26.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1+r_2 = \\boxed{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"100\" height=\"25\" /> as desired.\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><br />\nNote: It is necessary to check that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/6/ab6aab31d9871356a02b0d6042cd8d67e500269f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1-r_2\\ne 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"89\" height=\"18\" />, as you cannot divide by zero. As the problem states that the series are different, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/7/527eb0f0e7b75dc304574944e8893beb189a8d51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1 \\ne r_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" />, and so there is no division by zero error.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A\">2009 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2009 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017023141\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.037 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.053 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 289/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2298/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6949/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.485      1 -total\n 59.52%    7.431      1 Template:AMC12_box\n 38.79%    4.843      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:7793:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017023141 and revision id 199198. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}